    "answer": {
      "short": "$x^4-y^4=2x^2-1$.\n\nFactor the difference of squares, then substitute $x^2+y^2=1$ and $y^2=1-x^2$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^4-y^4&=(x^2-y^2)(x^2+y^2)\\\\x^4-y^4&=(x^2-y^2)\\cdot1\\\\x^4-y^4&=x^2-(1-x^2)\\\\x^4-y^4&=2x^2-1.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
